{
  "_about": "Which Spanish scopes (i18n_src/es/<scope>.json) and scripts each page uses. A page's bundle site/i18n/es.<page>.js is the merge of its scopes. 'scripts' are checked for T()/Tn()/Th() keys; 'data_labels' lists display strings that live in data files and reach the screen through T(variable). 'modules' are the parts of a page that load on first use: each has its own bundle site/i18n/es.<page>.<module>.js, loaded with I18N.load(module) by the module's loader, with the Spanish of its scopes and of every key its scripts ask for, less what the page bundle already holds. A data label spec's \"modules\" ({page: module}) puts its labels, on that page, in that module's bundle instead of the page's; a page's \"pick\" lists scopes shared with other pages of which its bundle takes only the keys its scripts ask for, its HTML shows or its own data labels need.",
